---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LANGS, type Lang, useT } from '../../i18n/ui';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return LANGS.map((lang) => ({ params: { lang } }));
}
const lang = Astro.params.lang as Lang;
const t = useT(lang);
---
<Base lang={lang} title={t('about.title')}>
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <header class="page-head"><h1>{t('about.title')}</h1></header>
    <div class="prose">
      {lang === 'zh-tw' ? (
        <>
          <p>這是一個中英雙語的教學網站，內容涵蓋數位影像處理、自然語言處理、圖形識別、機器學習與深度學習、電腦視覺、最佳化及資訊理論，從數學基礎一路講到近年的研究進展。</p>
          <p>每篇教學都先用淺白的比喻說明，再給出嚴謹的數學推導，並附上可以實際執行的 Python 程式碼、圖表、整理自綜述論文的「現代觀點」、練習題，以及經過查證的參考文獻。部分教學另有可以在瀏覽器中直接操作的互動示範，或可在 Google Colab 執行的 Jupyter 筆記本。</p>
          <p>可以從<a href="/zh-tw/learn/foundations/getting-started/">入門指南</a>開始，或直接到<a href="/zh-tw/learn/">學習</a>頁面挑選單元。</p>
          <h2>作者</h2>
          <p>本站由<strong>翁祥恩（Shyang-En Weng）</strong>建立與維護，目前為國立陽明交通大學資訊工程博士候選人，研究方向為影像處理、圖形識別與深度學習，專注於影像復原、低光影像增強與物件偵測。更多資訊請見個人網站 <a href="https://shyandram.dev/">shyandram.dev</a>。</p>
          <h2>本站如何製作</h2>
          <p>本站的內容與程式碼大多由 AI 模型建構：Anthropic 的 <strong>Claude</strong> 模型（透過 Claude Code，主要為 Claude Opus 5.5）與 OpenAI 的 <strong>GPT</strong> 模型（透過 Codex，主要為 GPT-6.1 Sol 與 GPT-6 Astra）。作者負責決定主題與課程架構、提供原始文章與研究素材，並審閱成果。</p>
          <p><strong>本站內容仍在審閱中。</strong>製作過程中，每篇參考文獻都經過連結與書目查證，程式碼也都實際執行過，但教學仍需要作者進一步檢查與修訂，可能有錯誤或疏漏。閱讀時請搭配原始文獻判斷；如果發現問題，歡迎到 <a href="https://github.com/Shyandram/cv-blog">GitHub</a> 回報。</p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>This is a bilingual (English / Traditional Chinese) tutorial site covering digital image processing, natural language processing, pattern recognition, machine learning and deep learning, computer vision, optimization and information theory, from the mathematical foundations to recent research.</p>
          <p>Every tutorial starts with a plain-language explanation, then gives the rigorous math, runnable Python code, figures, a "Modern view" built from survey papers, exercises, and verified references. Some tutorials also include interactive demos that run in your browser, or a Jupyter notebook you can open in Google Colab.</p>
          <p>Start with the <a href="/en/learn/foundations/getting-started/">getting-started guide</a>, or pick a track on the <a href="/en/learn/">Learn</a> page.</p>
          <h2>Author</h2>
          <p>This site is created and maintained by <strong>Shyang-En Weng (翁祥恩)</strong>, a PhD candidate in Computer Science at National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University (NYCU), Taiwan, working on image processing, pattern recognition and deep learning, with a focus on image restoration, low-light enhancement and object detection. More at <a href="https://shyandram.dev/">shyandram.dev</a>.</p>
          <h2>How this site was made</h2>
          <p>Most of the content and code on this site was constructed by AI models: Anthropic's <strong>Claude</strong> models (through Claude Code, mainly Claude Opus 5.5) and OpenAI's <strong>GPT</strong> models (through Codex, mainly GPT-6.1 Sol and GPT-6 Astra). The author chose the topics and course structure, supplied the original articles and research material, and reviewed the results.</p>
          <p><strong>This site is still under review.</strong> References were checked link by link and code was run before publishing, but the tutorials still need further checking and revision by the author, and they may contain mistakes or omissions. Please read them alongside the original sources; if you find a problem, report it on <a href="https://github.com/Shyandram/cv-blog">GitHub</a>.</p>
        </>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>.narrow { max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter)); }</style>
